msgctxt "speaker:Hugh"
msgid "Pay up or find some other fool that will risk a noose on you and your lady friend."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Captain Belmont"
msgid "Pay?"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Payback, she realized as she roughly continued fucking her mouth."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Paying the merchants, she carried the food items back to Jaeid's house."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Alfred"
msgid "Payment is by the end of every week. If you can't make it a full week, don't bother trying to collect any pay."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Payment, she realized."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Maeiv"
msgid "Peace can be an end in its own right."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Peace, both for her family and the ordinary people, could only come by hunting down the traitors."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Peace."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker-name"
msgid "Peasant girl"
msgstr "Ragazza contadina"

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Peasants, starved, will turn on their lords no matter their vows."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Peeling away at her armor, Sarah quickly managed to get rid of most of the obstacles in her way, leaving Kate naked."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Peering in through the narrow gap in the door, she could see most of them."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Peering into it, even from this distance, she could see the writhing masses of black shapeless tendrils."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Peering out from the window, Sarah saw the horrors that Xan had hoped to spare her."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Peering out into the darkness, for a moment, she saw only the shadows and shades of boxes and crates, remnants from the markets."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Peering out through the window, there was no movement out on the street. It was already dark and the city was sleeping."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Peering through her half-closed eyes, she saw his face in the moonlit dark."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Pelted with rocks, beaten with sticks, the townsfolk released their hatred."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Penetrating her exactly as deeply as she wanted. At the exact speed. The exact motion."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker-name"
msgid "People"
msgstr "Gente"

msgctxt "speaker:Alaric"
msgid "People all smiles cause it don't cost them shit, but when it comes down to it, people are out for themselves."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "People always had their own agenda's, but this was her decision to make."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Alaric"
msgid "People are all on guard, you can't just steal whatever."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Sigmund"
msgid "People been asking that question for as long as I can remember."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "People began to disperse."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Thomas"
msgid "People come up to me and ask me to settle disputes between noble houses I've never even heard of, or make military decisions, as if I know anything about that stuff..."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Thomas"
msgid "People come up to me. They keep asking me endless questions, expecting me to have the answer."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "People didn't seem to care here."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Hecate"
msgid "People die, they always do."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "People fell to their knees, weeping with abandon."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "People gambled out in the open."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "People gathered together, for warmth, for safety."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Garret"
msgid "People go in there, unprepared, they can end up lost. More than a few people found their deaths that way."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "People had begun to notice."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "People had build this, and lived here. All across the city, wonders rose up, and in the center, the greatest of all, a palace that seemed to shame any other in existence."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Lily"
msgid "People here are not...this isn't something that we can allow to exist."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "People like Varga made up most of the nation, it seemed absurd to Sarah that they should not have a voice at the table."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "People like to obsess. Give it a few day and they'll get around to something else."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "People looked, pointed and whispered."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "People of Calshure!"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "People of Rosanna!"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "People pretending to be something they weren't."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Sigmund"
msgid "People ripped others apart, murdered for the smallest of reasons, sometimes no reason at all."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "People roughly brushed up against her, uncaring to even so much as apologize or acknowledge."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Samayra"
msgid "People said that he used to be happier, but I never got to see that side of him."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Duke Antonio"
msgid "People see what they like to see. In me, they see a simple brute, who cares only for money."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Kate"
msgid "People smile, and say please, and do whatever you ask them."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Sophia"
msgid "People think they can't ever be slaves, but if you discipline them well enough, every man or woman got it in them to be a slave."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "People used to live here, and they had lived well. This was all that remained."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Alaric"
msgid "People were rushing down to the harbor along the main roads."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "People were tired. Exhausted."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Sigmund"
msgid "People will use whatever they can to get one over on you."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "People work, but even those that work make enough money to visit places like this."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "People! People lived their lives there! And they didn't deserve this..."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Guard"
msgid "People! There are people out there!"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "People, numbering more than a thousand, buzzing around in a mad orchestra."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "People, still running, screaming, stumbling as they madly tried to stay ahead of what was coming."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Per his invitation, Sarah arrived at Lord Edmond's chamber."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:King Orwell Rose"
msgid "Perceptive as always, daughter."
msgstr "Come sempre perspicace, figlia mia."

msgctxt "speaker:Razaphel"
msgid "Perceptive."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Xanthippe"
msgid "Perceptive. Putting your education to good use I see."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Vaelen"
msgid "Perfect!"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Perfect."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Perfect."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Maeiv"
msgid "Perfect. You always have to be perfect."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Perfectly shaped as her own body was."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Perhaps Dalia once had the same reservations, but had been trained to manage it over time."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Perhaps I am mad, but you and I are made for each other, so what does that say of you?"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Jaeid"
msgid "Perhaps I am more shocked."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Varga"
msgid "Perhaps I am tired."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Perhaps I could freshen up first, Captain?"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Razaphel"
msgid "Perhaps I have been too harsh on you."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Lily"
msgid "Perhaps I heard a sound."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Perhaps I only sought to escape the party."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Perhaps I should have been kinder to him when I said no..."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Perhaps I still am."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Perhaps I will consider painting your poor behavior as best I can."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Perhaps Jaeid was right. She found it hard to imagine respecting slave men such as these."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Perhaps Mary had been right, Sarah thought."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Perhaps Oliver had truly gotten wounded in a hunting accident, strange of a coincidence as it might be."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Perhaps Orc wives were made of stronger stuff, better able to endure the assault of an Orc male like Atilla."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Kravel"
msgid "Perhaps Queen Maeiv has extended this offer exactly for the reason that we might reject it."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Perhaps Sigmund was right in ignoring such stories."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Perhaps a bit of distraction was exactly what she needed."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Perhaps a council should rule."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Razaphel"
msgid "Perhaps a few minor revisions."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Perhaps a man like him needed more than one woman. Deserved more than one."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Perhaps a part of his concern was true. He did actually care for her safety."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Carolyn"
msgid "Perhaps a whipping or two, to set an example."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Perhaps all great men are a little bit mad, she wondered."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Perhaps all just a matter of perspective, Sarah thought as she could feel her mind slip into an early sleep."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Perhaps because she had relieved him the night earlier."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Perhaps begging might save her."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Perhaps by coincidence or fate, a woman just happened to walk past."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Perhaps eager to prove himself to her, or to do as she said and make the most of the time they had, whichever it was, Garret lasted long."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Perhaps even happier than usual."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Perhaps even just that was a statement aimed at her."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Perhaps even more just for the company than her skill with a blade."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Perhaps for the very first time, she saw him for the killer he was."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Perhaps had it been another, Sarah would have felt more cause to act offended, but in this place it only seemed natural."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Perhaps he enjoyed that too."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Perhaps he should retire."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Perhaps he was genuinely asking her a question. Perhaps he was testing her. Sarah could not be certain."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Perhaps he would have made a better King, but life had not played out like that."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Gilead"
msgid "Perhaps he would make for a better ally."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Perhaps if Alaric had been someone of importance, or meant something to someone, Sarah might have worried about the city guards."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Perhaps if she had been alone, she would have taken off her armor for the night."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Perhaps if she had just resigned herself to living a simpler life."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Perhaps if she had known how she had done it, she could celebrate, but now the whole affair was only strange to her."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Perhaps if she simply continued, her problem would resolve itself."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Perhaps if they had been anywhere other than this massive mansion, Sarah might have worried anyone would hear them."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Perhaps if they had been defeated in the battle, the men could have more easily carried their circumstance, but they had been victorious."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Gilead"
msgid "Perhaps if times were different, I would have settled this the old way."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Razaphel"
msgid "Perhaps if you are bored of talking, there are other things we could do."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Daemon"
msgid "Perhaps if you were too thick to understand before, you understand now?"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Lily"
msgid "Perhaps if you'd consider giving up your throne, I might consider taking you on as my squire."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Perhaps in Medini, such vows mean little to a whoring fiend like you, but I spoke them with all my heart."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Perhaps in Rosanna, the house would have seemed decent enough, something fitting for a skilled tradesmen."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Perhaps in a different life, she would have collected such a thing. Brought it back to Rosanna to show to her family."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Perhaps in a different world, she thought."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Perhaps in a way she was."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Perhaps in any other circumstance, she would have drawn more attention, but among the throng of naked bodies, hers was but one of many."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Perhaps in no small part, Sarah realized, because she now knew how they could pass their days instead."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Perhaps in this new world this was far from appropriate, but Sarah could not contain herself."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Marion"
msgid "Perhaps it can grow."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Perhaps it had been a while since he had known a woman's touch."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Perhaps it had been his proximity to her, but he had come to be less fearful of magic. Instead, he now seemed mostly interested by it."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Perhaps it had just been the madness of a man out at sea, or another way to torture Nick."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Marshal Edmond"
msgid "Perhaps it is simply conquest for the sake of it? History is not unfamiliar with men who write their names in blood."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Vaelen"
msgid "Perhaps it is your upbringing. Perhaps you were never taught how to learn your place."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Perhaps it was Atilla's fearsome appearance, or Sarah who ignored the world, but few people dared to say anything about their love."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Perhaps it was because she had seen her grow up around the castle and knew that so much of what Sarah pretended to be was just that, pretend."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Perhaps it was because she'd been here before."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Perhaps it was days, weeks, longer...she could no longer tell."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Perhaps it was even wise, given his experience as a general."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Perhaps it was her deep hunger, or perhaps there was something about this moment, but Sarah had rarely ever tasted anything quite this good."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Perhaps it was more his than hers, she thought as she crawled into the corner of the cage."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Perhaps it was the pressing of soft, expensive silk against her body, but Sarah's mind began to wander towards one way she knew of distracting her own mind."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Perhaps it was this fact that drove Sarah into the arms of the spirit."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Perhaps it was unfair to human men to be compared to an orc. Still, compared they were."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Perhaps it was unfamiliar to her, Sarah realized, but she did not pull away."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Perhaps it was, Sarah realized as they went deeper."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Perhaps it was, she thought, what did she really know if it."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Perhaps it was."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Perhaps it wasn't too late."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Perhaps it went some way to explaining the old man's endless appetite, taking what he could, knowing that out on war he might not get any."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Perhaps it would be wiser to end the night early."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Perhaps it would forget, though she doubted it would."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Perhaps it would have been better to die that day, together with her brother."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Perhaps it would have been wiser to call for a guard, but Sarah could not suppress her curiosity."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Perhaps it's bad luck, but yeah, I can feel it...somehow."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Marshal Edmond"
msgid "Perhaps knowing is overstating it, but I met him a few times before his untimely passing."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Perhaps more than even the dirt and grime of the desert, Sarah worried about the darkened look in her eyes."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Hassar"
msgid "Perhaps my mind is wandering in my old age."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Lily"
msgid "Perhaps my work here is done then."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Perhaps none had the answer."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Tribesman"
msgid "Perhaps not enough to keep the city, but enough to hurt your army. To weaken it for the real fight that awaits you at the capital. With Governor Kamal."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Perhaps not now. Perhaps not even in a month. But with how often he took her. How often he finished inside of her. It was only a matter of time."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Atilla"
msgid "Perhaps not, but I'm not looking for someone to follow me around. Go bother someone else."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Gilead"
msgid "Perhaps not."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Perhaps nothing could prepare her."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Vaelen"
msgid "Perhaps on that, we can agree."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Perhaps only the old knew of the carnage to come, but few soldiers lived to be old."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Perhaps only their rulers did not."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Perhaps other soldiers had seen what had happened, but in the chaos, they'd likely believe it was a figment of their imagination."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Perhaps our strategy was simply more sound than theirs."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Perhaps rejecting it had left its mark. Did it even have an ego to bruise? Sarah didn't know."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Perhaps she could learn to love that part of him, she joked to herself."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Perhaps she cried out for him like a woman gone mad. Perhaps she grinded her sex into him like a wild animal."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Perhaps she had been too cold to her friend. She knew what she wanted from her."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Perhaps she had been too harsh on the girl."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Perhaps she had died, she thought, and for her troubled life the gods had seen fit to reward her."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Perhaps she had gone mad. She wouldn't have been the first."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Perhaps she had gotten what she wanted in the end, if only by a different way."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Perhaps she might have been revolted by it, had it not been one of countless who had by now emptied himself into her mouth."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Perhaps she should have been sad for the loss of her words...but couldn't say why."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Perhaps she understood this girl better than most."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Perhaps she wanted to consider the past, because the future seemed so daunting."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Perhaps she was mad, she thought. How would she know."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Perhaps she was too strict on the girl."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Perhaps so, but still...to have so much when there is so much poverty, isn't that-"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Perhaps that had been what she first liked in Kate, Sarah realized."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Maeiv"
msgid "Perhaps that is my mistake."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Perhaps that was a better death than most could hope for in this world, she thought."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Perhaps that was dangerous as well, she thought. She didn't truly know the spirit or its intentions."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Perhaps the advantages of orcs in that department were simply impossible for a human male."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Perhaps the captain had a fraction of mercy in him left."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Perhaps the dead still think, but surely they don't suffer the minor annoyances of the living."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Perhaps the first time, she could have said something. But by now, what was her excuse?"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Perhaps the girl would be alright after all."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Perhaps the gods did listen to her, she wondered."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Perhaps the old soldier was kind, and perhaps part of him did want to save her. But he was no knight. He wanted her for what she had used to seduce him into buying her in the first place. Her body."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Perhaps the others believe him. Perhaps they simply go along with him. The result is the same."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Perhaps the sight of her pleasure, or perhaps having reached his own limit; whichever it was, Sarah heard him groan deeply."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Perhaps the spirit had only told her enough truth to twist her to it's own designs."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Razaphel"
msgid "Perhaps the time for talking is over."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Perhaps the two are not so different."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Perhaps the world had beaten that out of her."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Perhaps the world had known larger armies. Perhaps it had known better armed and trained armies."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Perhaps then you can build a nation where such things can be."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Perhaps there was a pattern to the chaos, but she had not yet managed to resolve it."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Perhaps there was an advantage to be had for her in that. In knowing him."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Perhaps there was some truth in it, she realized."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Perhaps there was some truth to it. She'd spend all her life protecting Thomas from the small problems, now she'd need to learn to keep him safe from the great dangers."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Perhaps there was some vanity to it, but Sarah equally knew that men had a habit of treating her better when she looked her best."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Perhaps there was something to Sakar's words. Perhaps if she could get to know the man, she'd have a better estimate of him."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Perhaps there weren't many words because there wasn't much left to say."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Perhaps there would be something in her room that might aid her."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Razaphel"
msgid "Perhaps these Gods might have denied her, but what if there were others Gods out there? Some who might look favorably on her request?"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Perhaps they had been beaten too badly to try again."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Perhaps they had dug in too deep, or perhaps the Bagrad army was stretched too thin trying to defend the city's main gate from falling."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Perhaps they had that in common too."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Perhaps they knew more of what this was about."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Perhaps they knew something instinctively, that humans by reason had forgotten."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Metis"
msgid "Perhaps they were always like that."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Perhaps they were not so different from herself."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Perhaps they were shops, what did she really know of this place, Sarah thought to herself."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Perhaps they were."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Perhaps they'd have to be released before they returned to Lethram, but Sarah could see most were content if only to own slaves for the moment."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Perhaps this man was a possible solution."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
